   {
    "text": "In the realm of verse and rhythm, where words take flight and minds are stirred,  \nThere lies a guide, a sage, a scribe of thought,  \nWho teaches us the art of craft, the craft of art,  \nAnd how to write with flair, with grace, with heart.  \n\nThis is the *ars poetica*, the ancient art of verse,  \nA guide for poets, a map for those who seek.  \nIt speaks of form, of meter, of rhyme, of style,  \nAnd how to craft a poem that will never die.  \n\nBut now, I present a tale of wit and whims,  \nA jest upon the art of writing, a mock and mild.  \nFor in this world, where words are power, and words are gold,  \nWe must not fear the craft, but mock the bold.  \n\nThe *ars poetica* is but a shadow, a tale,  \nA guide that leads to nowhere, a tale that's all.  \nIt speaks of meter, of rhyme, of rhythm, of line,  \nBut in the end, it's just a joke, a joke, a fine.  \n\nSo let us not take it too seriously, nor too lightly,  \nFor in the end, it's all a game, a game of wit.  \nA poem is but a spark, a fleeting flame,  \nA moment of truth, a moment of flame.  \n\nAnd so, we write, we craft, we dream, we play,  \nWith words that dance, with lines that sing, with flair.  \nFor in the end, the *ars poetica* is but a tale,  \nA guide for those who dare to write, to play, to fail.",
